This project incorporates code from the following open-source projects.
Their licence terms are reproduced in third_party/ and apply to the files named
below. Everything not named here was written for this project.

================================================================================
CoST -- Contrastive Learning of Disentangled Seasonal-Trend Representations
        for Time Series Forecasting
================================================================================
Copyright (c) 2022, Salesforce.com, Inc.
Licence: BSD 3-Clause  (third_party/LICENSE.CoST)
Source:  https://github.com/salesforce/CoST
Paper:   Gerald Woo, Chenghao Liu, Doyen Sahoo, Akshat Kumar, Steven Hoi.
         ICLR 2022.  arXiv:2202.01575

Derived files and components:
  cost.py             CoST / CoSTModel, the MoCo trend branch (momentum encoder,
                      key queue, compute_loss, _dequeue_and_enqueue), the
                      seasonal instance-contrastive term, convert_coeff, and the
                      encode / _eval_with_pooling inference path.
  models/encoder.py   CoSTEncoder and BandedFourierLayer.
  utils.py            init_dl_program, split_with_nan,
                      centerize_vary_length_series, torch_pad_nan.
  data_processing/    the calendar-covariate construction, which follows
                      CoST's datautils._get_time_features field for field.

All of the above are MODIFIED. The modifications are listed in README.md under
"What is ours"; the most substantial are a frequency-domain readout of the
seasonal branch, a unit-circle embedding of the seasonal phase inside the loss,
a per-harmonic banding of the Fourier layer, and alternative positive-pair and
negative-sampling schemes. None of these are present upstream.

================================================================================
TS2Vec -- Towards Universal Representation of Time Series
================================================================================
Copyright (c) 2022 Zhihan Yue
Licence: MIT  (third_party/LICENSE.TS2Vec)
Source:  https://github.com/zhihanyue/ts2vec
Paper:   Zhihan Yue et al.  AAAI 2022.  arXiv:2106.10466

Derived files and components, which reached this project through CoST:
  models/dilated_conv.py    SamePadConv, ConvBlock, DilatedConvEncoder --
                            the dilated-convolution backbone, unmodified except
                            for the final projection width.
  cost.py                   instance_contrastive_loss, the within-batch
                            instance-discrimination term the seasonal branch
                            uses. Modified: it is applied to the unit-circle
                            phase embedding rather than to raw angles, and the
                            negatives it scores against are selectable.

